{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q48318","formula":"CH₄N₂O","hill":"CH4N2O","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":1.0,"H":4.0,"N":2.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"Urea","ru":"Мочевина","uk":"Сечовина"},"descriptions":{"en":"Urea, also called carbamide (because it is a diamide of carbonic acid), is an organic compound with chemical formula CO(NH2)2. This amide has two amino groups (−NH2) joined by a carbonyl functional group (−C(=O)−). It is thus the simplest amide of carbamic acid.","ru":"Мочеви́на (карбамид, урея) — химическое соединение, диамид угольной кислоты. Белые кристаллы, растворимые в полярных растворителях (воде, этаноле, жидком аммиаке).","uk":"Сечови́на або карбамід — CO(NH2)2, діамід вуглецевої кислоти, білі кристали, добре розчинні у воді. Карбамід не є ні кислим, ні лужним."},"fame":85,"pubchemCid":1176,"mass":60.056,"charge":0,"smiles":"C(=O)(N)N","inchikey":"XSQUKJJJFZCRTK-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"urea","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"1176","atoms":8,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.304,"y":-0.001,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":0.69,"y":-1.148,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":0.689,"y":1.149,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.075,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":1.704,"y":-1.111,"z":0.0,"el":"H"},{"x":0.261,"y":-2.067,"z":0.0,"el":"H"},{"x":0.258,"y":2.067,"z":0.0,"el":"H"},{"x":1.703,"y":1.113,"z":0.0,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,3,2],[1,3,1],[1,4,1],[1,5,1],[2,3,1],[2,6,1],[2,7,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q48318","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Urea","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9C%D0%BE%D1%87%D0%B5%D0%B2%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B0","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}